My gut reaction is that the graphic photos would make me wince the first couple of times, but I'd get used to them quickly, like with cigarette packs. The calorie badges are what would actually change what I pick, because I could compare a 95 calorie fruit pot with a 240 calorie Dairy Milk on the spot. Warnings with no numbers feel preachy and give me nothing to act on. And when it's the same snacks with no labels, nothing changes at all.

Calorie badges on everything (C) give me real information. Adding the text warning (B) is a bit nagging but harmless, and adding the graphic photo (D) gives a bit of extra shock on top of the numbers. A and E tell me nothing I can use, so they'd barely register.

