Gut reaction: I'm a normal bloke who grabs a snack without much thought. Calorie badges are the only thing that gives me usable information at the point of choice, so seeing 240 next to 95 might nudge me a bit. The graphic photos would make me wince, and maybe put me off for a day or two, but I'd soon get used to them and find them annoying. The plain text warning is just wallpaper, and I'd scroll past it. The no-label option does nothing at all.

Of the schemes, C probably has the most immediate effect because the photo is hard to ignore and the calorie badge gives me something to act on. D is similar but without the numbers, so it's less useful. A is the quiet, practical option and the one I'd keep noticing without resenting. B adds a text warning that I'd ignore. E and F would do almost nothing.

