Gut reaction: I'd mostly shrug at the warnings. I know crisps and chocolate aren't good for me, and a plain text warning would just become wallpaper like the ones on fags. The graphic photos would make me wince, and maybe put me off once or twice, but I'd get used to them or just avoid looking. The calorie numbers are the thing that actually gives me something to compare, because a lot of the "healthy" stuff is not much lower than the treats. Seeing 240 next to 95 would make me think twice, especially if I'm trying to keep an eye on my weight.

C combines both, so it would probably have the biggest effect on me, with the photo adding a bit of a shock on top of the numbers. B and F are close behind, since the calorie badge does most of the work. A and E have no numbers, so I'd mostly ignore them. D is nothing at all.

