Gut reaction: I'm a man in my late 50s or 60s and I don't much like being nagged. Calorie badges are practical, so I'd glance at them and maybe think twice, since "240 vs 95" is easy to see. The graphic photos would put me off at first, and I'd probably find them a bit much, but they would make me look away from the high-calorie stuff. Plain text warnings I'd scroll past, because I've seen it all on fag packets and wine labels. No labels at all changes nothing.

Honestly, the combination of photo and calorie count (E) would push me hardest. The photo gives the shock, and the number lets me compare and choose something else instead of just feeling grim. Calorie badges on their own (A) would nudge me a bit, and (B) a bit more. The photo with no calories (D) would still work, but less well because I'd have nothing to switch to.

